---
/* ============================================================
   Our Journey — mist band, a three-chapter horizontal timeline
   ------------------------------------------------------------
   Three equal columns across the 1184px container with a 32px gutter,
   and a 1px rail running the full width behind them. The export gave
   the columns as absolutely-positioned boxes at left 0 / 405.33 /
   810.66 with three stacked spacers behind them; that arithmetic is a
   3 × 373.33 grid with a 32px gap, and it is built as a grid.

   THE RAIL PASSES THROUGH THE MARKERS. The export put it 12px below
   them, which reads as a stray line rather than a timeline; the markers
   carry a 3px mist border, so on this band they punch a clean hole in
   the rail wherever they sit on it. Logged in OPEN-QUESTIONS.md #15.

   THE MARKERS ARE SQUARE, and this is the one place where the export
   and the design system flatly contradict each other. The export draws
   the markers as circles, with the pill-shaped corner utility on them.
   DESIGN-SYSTEM §0 rule 2 forbids a corner radius anywhere and enforces
   it with a grep that must return nothing — so building the export
   literally would fail a build gate twice over: once for the property,
   and once because this very comment would compile the utility it named
   into the shipped stylesheet, which is the trap the note at the top of
   tokens.css is about. Squared, flagged, and written up as the first
   item of OPEN-QUESTIONS.md #16.

   The 2px teal ring around each marker IS kept, even though §11 reserves
   teal for project badges, because it is the only thing that makes the
   marker visible: a mint mark on mist is the 1.2:1 problem of
   OPEN-QUESTIONS.md #1, and a designer reaching for a second colour
   here looks like a fix for exactly that. Also #16.

   RESOLVED, #1: every mint element on this band — the marker fill, the
   `CHAPTER I` labels, the bullet marks, and the Kicker — now uses
   `--kd-mint-2`. The teal ring stays; it was doing real work, and the
   darker fill only makes the marker read better inside it.

   BELOW `lg` THE TIMELINE RUNS DOWN THE PAGE. Three columns need about
   290px each to hold a chapter; under 1024 they do not have it. The
   chapters stack, the rail turns to run down the left edge through the
   same markers, and each chapter's copy is set in 40px from it. From
   `lg` up it is the row described above, unchanged.
   ============================================================ */
import { about } from "../../data/about";
import Kicker from "../Kicker.astro";

const { journey } = about;
---

<section class="bg-kd-mist py-96">
  <div class="max-w-kd mx-auto px-24 sm:px-48">
    <Kicker label={journey.kicker} editKey="about.journey.kicker" tone="light" />

    <h2
      class="font-display text-d4 text-kd-ink mt-16"
      data-edit="about.journey.heading"
    >
      {journey.heading}
    </h2>

    <div class="relative mt-56">
      {/* Behind the chapters, centred on the 16px markers: across the
          row from `lg`, down the left edge below it. */}
      <span
        class="absolute bg-kd-divider-light max-lg:inset-y-0 max-lg:left-8 max-lg:w-1 lg:inset-x-0 lg:top-8 lg:h-1"
        aria-hidden="true"></span>

      <ol class="relative grid grid-cols-1 gap-48 lg:grid-cols-3 lg:gap-32">
        {
          journey.chapters.map((chapter, i) => (
            <li class="max-lg:relative max-lg:pl-40">
              <span
                class="block max-lg:absolute max-lg:left-0 max-lg:top-0 size-16 bg-kd-mint-2 border-[3px] border-kd-mist outline-2 outline-kd-teal"
                aria-hidden="true"
              />

              <p
                class="text-num uppercase text-kd-mint-2 lg:mt-32"
                data-edit={`about.journey.chapters.${i}.chapter`}
              >
                {chapter.chapter}
              </p>

              <h3
                class="font-display text-d7 text-kd-ink mt-8"
                data-edit={`about.journey.chapters.${i}.title`}
              >
                {chapter.title}
              </h3>

              <p
                class="text-label uppercase text-kd-slate mt-6"
                data-edit={`about.journey.chapters.${i}.phase`}
              >
                {chapter.phase}
              </p>

              <ul class="mt-20 flex flex-col gap-8">
                {chapter.points.map((point, j) => (
                  <li class="flex items-start gap-8">
                    <span
                      class="block size-6 bg-kd-mint-2 shrink-0 mt-6"
                      aria-hidden="true"
                    />
                    <span
                      class="text-body-sm text-kd-slate-2"
                      data-edit={`about.journey.chapters.${i}.points.${j}`}
                    >
                      {point}
                    </span>
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
